  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">English &amp; School Education: Empowerment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowerment is one of the Global Programmes through which the British Council delivers its grant-funded activity. The primary focus of this Global Programme is ODA eligible activity and outcomes.The Empowerment programme supports resilience and agency, building positive pathways through English language and life skills at times of crises, focusing on disadvantaged groups. The priority themes include: &#x25fc;English in education, &#x25fc;Teaching quality, &#x25fc;Crisis, displacement and migration, &#x25fc;Girls&#x2019; education, &#x25fc;Life skills for young peopleThere are four areas of focus for this programme: 1) Capacity Building, 2) Research and insight, 3) Stakeholder engagement and, 4) Technical advice for teaching and learning resources.&#x25fc; 1. Capacity building :&#x25fe; 1.1 of teachers to support themselves and their learners at times of crisis and/or forced displacement, to access resources and peer networks&#x25fe; 1.2 of disadvantaged girls and young women through safe learning spaces and curricula and resources for English and other skills.&#x25fe; 1.3 of educators of young people to develop English and skills for employment.&#x25fc; 2. Research and insight&#x25fc; 3. Stakeholder engagement&#x25fc; 4. Technical advice for teaching and learning resourcesWhy we do it:&#x25fc;Enhanced ability for individuals to access decent work, social well-being, voice, influence, agency and control over their lives and the institutions that affect them&#x25fc;Improved community resilience through empowered vulnerable individuals and the parents and educators that support them&#x25fc;Improved understanding of how language can support cohesion and peace&#x25fc;Institutions and organisations working with marginalised youth women and girls and displaced people can better support these people and have in the British Council a trusted partner.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The target audiences for this programme are: &#x25fc; Displaced people and disadvantaged youth &#x25fc; Women and girls&#x25fc; Educators and learning facilitators&#x25fc; Partnerships between local and international institutions</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x25fc; 1. Displaced people and disadvantaged youth have improved language and other life skills to enable agency and access to resources and opportunity.&#x25fc; 2. Women and girls have improved language, life skills, confidence and agency to access opportunities in their communities.&#x25fc; 3. Educators and learning facilitators have developed capacity to support disadvantaged learners and accessed networks to share best practice.&#x25fc; 4. Partnerships between local and international institutions contribute to understanding of and support for language and other skills as enablers for disadvantaged groups.</narrative>
  </description>
